cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "BUSCOmega: a BUSCO dN/dS pipeline for a per-species Ne proxy"
abstract: >-
  BUSCOmega turns per-species BUSCO output into a per-species effective
  population size (Ne) proxy. It finds the single-copy orthologs common to
  every species in a clade, codon-aligns them (MAFFT then PAL2NAL), runs
  codeml (PAML) under a two-ratio branch model with each species in turn as
  the foreground, and pools per-gene synonymous and nonsynonymous
  substitution across genes into one count-pooled dN/dS per lineage with a
  gene-bootstrap confidence interval. Developed as part of dissertation work
  on the identification and evolutionary analysis of de novo genes (DNGs).
  Standard-library Python only.
authors:
